{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1010720-i-need-to-ask-something-highly-controversial-topic-please-be-patient-with-me","id":1010720,"title":"i need to ask something. (Highly-controversial topic. Please be patient with me)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-01T11:19:57-08:00","id":1010720,"title":"i need to ask something. (Highly-controversial topic. Please be patient with me)","content":"Okay,i need to vent a bit and if any of you guys could answer that'd be fine. So, all cards on the table. I'm anti-abortion. i tried not to be but the truth is. When i see an abortion,i see a little kind being thrown in thrash-bin. I see . My country,Brazil, had some reviews our laws this week. it was bad,but one law i do agree with is the Criminizalition of abortion unless the pregnancy directs threatens the woman's life. It is hard for me seeing so many people railing against politicians who voted for that. Especially because those people didnt attack politicians who did worse. And it's hard for me to understand something about pro-choice people. Why do you think people who are against abortion are just trying to hurt women? every single pro-choice argument i've sen always says &quot;you don't care about women,You just want to hurt women&quot;. And that's just isn't the reality. Based on my experiences almost all pro-life people are coming from the same idea. That a fetus is a human being, or at the very least will become a human being and that we shouldn't let people just thrown them away like that. I'm still trying to understand pro-choice to empathize with them. that's why i'm asking this here,please be patient with.<br /> <br /> Why is there a belief that pro-life people about trying to hurt woman and not about saving lifes, or at the very least things that will be alive after some months?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 12-01-2016, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T11:42:30-08:00","id":1010727,"title":"","content":"Because if there aren't god-tier adoption services available, free medical care for the woman while she's pregnant to assist with the pregnancy and delivery, and post-natal care for both the woman, child, and father to ensure that an unwanted pregnancy won't disrupt their lives too much, and strong social services for families with young children, and laws against rapists getting parental rights, then anybody who claims they're pro-life stinks of hypocrisy to me. At that point you're just pro-birth and if you're going to require women to carry a pregnancy to term without helping her out with it then you don't deserve to call yourself pro-life.<br /> <br /> Also, sometimes things get heated. Even if you're not anti-women, you at least don't care about how women feel if you force them to carry a pregnancy to term. Saying a woman must go through with a pregnancy is taking away their rights to their own bodies and futures. If that's secondary to the child's life to you, then you can understand why some women find that abhorrent.<br /> <br /> So, in short, I'm only okay with making abortion unavailable if:<br /> 1) Adoption is painless and easy and all pregnancy-related costs prior to the adoption are covered by the state (and afterwards as well, to make sure the mother stays healthy)<br /> 2) The mother will not suffer physically, monetarily, politically, or socially for having the child<br /> 3) If the child is a product of rape, then the rapist <b><i>WILL NOT EVER</i></b> be able to see or interact with the child in a meaningful way other than child support payments<br /> 4) Guaranteed parental leave for the first...I dunno, let's say 6 months to a year. This must be for any parents involved.<br /> 5) If there's a significant threat to the woman's life, the pregnancy has to be able to be terminated. There will be no one's opinion on this other than the mother's considered. They get final say.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't believe a fetus is a person or even really alive in a meaningful sense for at least a few months. So at that point all I hear from the pro-life crowd is &quot;You have to sacrifice your well-being for this wad of tissue that may kill or at least seriously disadvantage you in a way that men will never have to deal with.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T11:43:55-08:00","id":1010728,"title":"","content":"So for context I myself used to be pro-life, but have over the years changed position to be strongly pro-choice.<br /> <br /> You are correct in noticing that both sides of the abortion debate tend to talk past each other a lot. You are also correct in picking out the &quot;personhood&quot; question as being central to the problem. I think the reason for the former is in large part because of the latter. The argument over what constitutes &quot;personhood&quot; frequently comes down to questions of subjective philosophy rather than objective biology. That tends to make it something you either believe or don't, or at the very least you either prioritize or don't. Since there isn't really any give to be had on that particular front, the debate shifts into the other areas that get wrapped up in the larger abortion question: bodily autonomy, women's rights, sexual mores, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T11:51:17-08:00","id":1010736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1010720-i-need-to-ask-something-highly-controversial-topic-please-be-patient-with-me?p=1010727#post1010727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because if there aren't god-tier adoption services available, free medical care for the woman while she's pregnant to assist with the pregnancy and delivery, and post-natal care for both the woman, child, and father to ensure that an unwanted pregnancy won't disrupt their lives too much, and strong social services for families with young children, and laws against rapists getting parental rights, then anybody who claims they're pro-life stinks of hypocrisy to me. At that point you're just pro-birth and if you're going to require women to carry a pregnancy to term without helping her out with it then you don't deserve to call yourself pro-life.<br /> <br /> Also, sometimes things get heated. Even if you're not anti-women, you at least don't care about how women feel if you force them to carry a pregnancy to term. Saying a woman must go through with a pregnancy is taking away their rights to their own bodies and futures. If that's secondary to the child's life to you, then you can understand why some women find that abhorrent.<br /> <br /> So, in short, I'm only okay with making abortion unavailable if:<br /> 1) Adoption is painless and easy and all pregnancy-related costs prior to the adoption are covered by the state (and afterwards as well, to make sure the mother stays healthy)<br /> 2) The mother will not suffer physically, monetarily, politically, or socially for having the child<br /> 3) If the child is a product of rape, then the rapist <b><i>WILL NOT EVER</i></b> be able to see or interact with the child in a meaningful way other than child support payments<br /> 4) Guaranteed parental leave for the first...I dunno, let's say 6 months to a year. This must be for any parents involved.<br /> 5) If there's a significant threat to the woman's life, the pregnancy has to be able to be terminated. There will be no one's opinion on this other than the mother's considered. They get final say.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't believe a fetus is a person or even really alive in a meaningful sense for at least a few months. So at that point all I hear from the pro-life crowd is &quot;You have to sacrifice your well-being for this wad of tissue that may kill or at least seriously disadvantage you in a way that men will never have to deal with.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we as a society could make your 5 points a reality. I do agree with allowing abortions in a life death situations Because if i was locked ina room that was about to explode and the only way to get out would be killing someone,i think i might do it. but doing that in almost any other situation should be illegal.<br /> One situation that really made me mad last year was i found out someone i idolized aborted and their reason was &quot;I still wanted to go to parties and live my life only for myself and not lose any money&quot;. Those were their words, not mine. Even if they didnt believe a fetus is a person,they still threw away something that was going to be a person because they wanted to go to parties. that's the pro-choicers i'm afraid of.<br /> I do have to disagree with &quot;the mother will not suffer monetarily&quot;. No money is worth that much and that's coming from someone who has poor for a very long time and suffered depression because of his poverty.<br /> Also, if you wanted to know my reasoning for seeing fetuses as people. it's because they have a brain,they can think. no matter how base their thoughts are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 12-01-2016, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T11:55:29-08:00","id":1010738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1010720-i-need-to-ask-something-highly-controversial-topic-please-be-patient-with-me?p=1010728#post1010728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So for context I myself used to be pro-life, but have over the years changed position to be strongly pro-choice.<br /> <br /> You are correct in noticing that both sides of the abortion debate tend to talk past each other a lot. You are also correct in picking out the &quot;personhood&quot; question as being central to the problem. I think the reason for the former is in large part because of the latter. The argument over what constitutes &quot;personhood&quot; frequently comes down to questions of subjective philosophy rather than objective biology. That tends to make it something you either believe or don't, or at the very least you either prioritize or don't. Since there isn't really any give to be had on that particular front, the debate shifts into the other areas that get wrapped up in the larger abortion question: bodily autonomy, women's rights, sexual mores, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you there,many pro-lifers are acting out of prejudice and downright mysoginy instead of trying to protect people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T11:56:06-08:00","id":1010739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1010720-i-need-to-ask-something-highly-controversial-topic-please-be-patient-with-me?p=1010736#post1010736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we as a society could make your 5 points a reality. I do agree with allowing abortions in a life death situations Because if i was locked ina room that was about to explode and the only way to get out would be killing someone,i think i might do it. but doing that in almost any other situation should be illegal.<br /> One situation that really made me mad last year was i found out someone i idolized aborted and their reason was &quot;I still wanted to go to parties and live my life only for myself&quot; their words not mine. Even if they didnt believe a fetus is a person,they still threw away something that was going to be a person because they wanted to go to parties. that's the pro-choicers i'm afraid of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, personally I think that's their right. It might seem cold, but my stance on it is this: &quot;If a child-bearing person decides that for whatever reason having a child will negatively impact their life, livelihood, or future, they shouldn't be forced to have a child.&quot; That's why I won't compromise on my 5 points. Nobody should have the responsibility of another life forced upon them, so either we say &quot;Okay, then you have the right to not bring that life into the world.&quot; or we make it so that it isn't a burden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T11:58:20-08:00","id":1010740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1010720-i-need-to-ask-something-highly-controversial-topic-please-be-patient-with-me?p=1010739#post1010739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, personally I think that's their right. It might seem cold, but my stance on it is this: &quot;If a child-bearing person decides that for whatever reason having a child will negatively impact their life, livelihood, or future, they shouldn't be forced to have a child.&quot; That's why I won't compromise on my 5 points. Nobody should have the responsibility of another life forced upon them, so either we say &quot;Okay, then you have the right to not bring that life into the world.&quot; or we make it so that it isn't a burden.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's putting someone for ana doption that hard in your country? In mine,despite many social problems, it's kinda easy,it had a whole tv show about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T12:01:22-08:00","id":1010745,"title":"","content":"I think the perception that all pro-life people hate/don't care about women is pretty much the same as the perception that all pro-choice people hate/don't care about babies. Both are mostly rhetoric designed to smear the opposing side, and I don't think either is really true of the majority of people on either side. Ultimately people fall on one side or the other for altruistic reasons; it's just a matter of different values. The problem with criminalizing abortions, in my opinion, is that it doesn't stop them. It just makes them more dangerous for the woman. If you want to protect unborn babies, better sex education is a more effective way to do that. Reducing unwanted and unintended pregancies will do more to reduce abortions than criminalizing them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T12:03:31-08:00","id":1010747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1010720-i-need-to-ask-something-highly-controversial-topic-please-be-patient-with-me?p=1010745#post1010745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to protect unborn babies, better sex education is a more effective way to do that. Reducing unwanted and unintended pregancies will do more to reduce abortions than criminalizing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dangit, sex education, I knew I was missing a bullet in my list. It's super important.<br /> <br /> EDIT: A part &quot;good sex education&quot; includes never teaching abstinence-only. Birth control should be freely accessible by everybody, and child-bearing people shouldn't be punished if the birth control doesn't work. Again: If a child-bearing person doesn't want a child, then they should not be forced to have a child for any reason, including mistakes. And pre-marital sex better not count as a mistake, or as something worth punishing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":1923,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","user":"BigDamnHero","date":". 12-01-2016, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T12:11:22-08:00","id":1010752,"title":"","content":"I was pro-life and frankly, I still think abortion is morally wrong, but now I am pro-choice. This is what changed my mind:<br /> <br /> I had a close friend in college who had an abortion. Giving birth and giving up the child would have been emotionally devastating to her. She was not the most emotionally stable person and would have most likely committed suicide in that situation. She wavered a lot about whether she should keep the child. She was 18 years old, had poor taste in men, and was unemployed. If she had the child, she would have been had trapped in an emotionally abusive relationship (because being the mother of his child constituted ownership to the father's point of view). She couldn't give the child the best life possible. <br /> <br /> Now, not knowing her personally, it would be easy to say &quot;Oh, she should have known better. She should have not had sex if she didn't understand the consequences.&quot; or &quot;She should have stuck it up and given it up for adoption.&quot;<br /> <br /> But you don't know. You haven't had to watch your friend suffer though this decision. When she asked me what I thought, I didn't give her the spiel I learned in Catholic school. All those words seemed heartless in her case. Instead I told her it was her decision and I would support whatever she did. I even talked to a mutual friend who was also Pro-Life and we both agreed that the friend's situation was special. She wasn't like <i>those women</i> we were taught in Catholic school. <br /> <br /> So I went on with my life. Still pro-life, in spite of advising my friend to make her own choice. in my defense, I wasn't completely heartless. I was pro-birth control. I support increased social services. But I drew the line at abortion. <br /> <br /> Then I read <a href=\"http://www.prochoiceactionnetwork-canada.org/articles/anti-tales.shtml\" target=\"_blank\">the only mortal abortion is my own abortion</a>. And I saw the same excuses I made for supporting my friend reflected in those stories. Obviously, their situation was different. The same words I used all those years ago with my friend. That is when I realized every situation is different when you are living it. That the decision to end a pregnancy should be between a woman and her doctor. I, nor the government, had no place in that decision. <br /> <br /> To look at this from another point of view, consider end of life care. The decision to end life support is left with the family or the individual if they wrote a living will. From a certain point of view, not doing everything in your power to help an individual live could be considered murder. Yet this highly personal decision is not decided by the government. <br /> <br /> Just like from a certain point of view, people consider ending the pregnancy murder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T12:14:46-08:00","id":1010755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1010720-i-need-to-ask-something-highly-controversial-topic-please-be-patient-with-me?p=1010740#post1010740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's putting someone for ana doption that hard in your country? In mine,despite many social problems, it's kinda easy,it had a whole tv show about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I live in the US.<br /> <br /> If you are white baby, it is easy to find a home. Most people who wish to adopt want a child that sort of looks like them. And most of the people who have money to adopt are white. Thus white babies are easy. But those aren't the only children who need a home. If you aren't white, you could be giving birth to a baby and sending them to foster care.<br /> <br /> (FYI, my friend in my previous post was Hispanic. )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 12-01-2016, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T12:30:38-08:00","id":1010765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1010720-i-need-to-ask-something-highly-controversial-topic-please-be-patient-with-me?p=1010752#post1010752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was pro-life and frankly, I still think abortion is morally wrong, but now I am pro-choice. This is what changed my mind:<br /> <br /> I had a close friend in college who had an abortion. Giving birth and giving up the child would have been emotionally devastating to her. She was not the most emotionally stable person and would have most likely committed suicide in that situation. She wavered a lot about whether she should keep the child. She was 18 years old, had poor taste in men, and was unemployed. If she had the child, she would have been had trapped in an emotionally abusive relationship (because being the mother of his child constituted ownership to the father's point of view). She couldn't give the child the best life possible. <br /> <br /> Now, not knowing her personally, it would be easy to say &amp;quot;Oh, she should have known better. She should have not had sex if she didn't understand the consequences.&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;She should have stuck it up and given it up for adoption.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> But you don't know. You haven't had to watch your friend suffer though this decision. When she asked me what I thought, I didn't give her the spiel I learned in Catholic school. All those words seemed heartless in her case. Instead I told her it was her decision and I would support whatever she did. I even talked to a mutual friend who was also Pro-Life and we both agreed that the friend's situation was special. She wasn't like <i>those women</i> we were taught in Catholic school. <br /> <br /> So I went on with my life. Still pro-life, in spite of advising my friend to make her own choice. in my defense, I wasn't completely heartless. I was pro-birth control. I support increased social services. But I drew the line at abortion. <br /> <br /> Then I read <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.prochoiceactionnetwork-canada.org/articles/anti-tales.shtml&amp;quot;]the</a> only mortal abortion is my own abortion[/URL]. And I saw the same excuses I made for supporting my friend reflected in those stories. Obviously, their situation was different. The same words I used all those years ago with my friend. That is when I realized every situation is different when you are living it. That the decision to end a pregnancy should be between a woman and her doctor. I, nor the government, had no place in that decision. <br /> <br /> To look at this from another point of view, consider end of life care. The decision to end life support is left with the family or the individual if they wrote a living will. From a certain point of view, not doing everything in your power to help an individual live could be considered murder. Yet this highly personal decision is not decided by the government. <br /> <br /> Just like from a certain point of view, people consider ending the pregnancy murder.</div> </div> </div> </div>The choice she had to make was either wrecking her Life or taking away the Life of another. I still think she didnt made a Good choice. All the things that would have happened to herbif she cart\u00f5es the birth could be fixed she could have dodged the guy, she could have solved it somehow it's a huge maybe but it's still possible. Theres no mayb,for the kid no other possibility. The kid has no Life and thats it.<br /> S\u00f3 if the choice is wrecking your Life or aborting. Wreck it. your Life can be fixed,the kid cant regain the life they lost","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T12:36:10-08:00","id":1010768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1010720-i-need-to-ask-something-highly-controversial-topic-please-be-patient-with-me?p=1010765#post1010765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The choice she had to make was either wrecking her Life or taking away the Life of another. I still think she didnt made a Good choice. All the things that would have happened to herbif she cart\u00f5es the birth could be fixed she could have dodged the guy, she could have solved it somehow it's a huge maybe but it's still possible. Theres no mayb,for the kid no other possibility. The kid has no Life and thats it.<br /> S\u00f3 if the choice is wrecking your Life or aborting. Wreck it. your Life can be fixed,the kid cant regain the life they lost</div> </div> </div> </div>You also have to consider the possibility that no life might be better for the (potential) kid than the life they would be stuck with as a result of the situation they would be born into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T12:41:00-08:00","id":1010769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1010720-i-need-to-ask-something-highly-controversial-topic-please-be-patient-with-me?p=1010768#post1010768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You also have to consider the possibility that no life might be better for the (potential) kid than the life they would be stuck with as a result of the situation they would be born into.</div> </div> </div> </div>People esccape from horrible situations all the time. I think is better to be born into an horrible situation and having a chance to escape than to never have a life","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T12:44:20-08:00","id":1010771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1010720-i-need-to-ask-something-highly-controversial-topic-please-be-patient-with-me?p=1010768#post1010768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You also have to consider the possibility that no life might be better for the (potential) kid than the life they would be stuck with as a result of the situation they would be born into.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of a dark argument. I know some people who were born to pretty brutal situations who have ended up having happy and successful lives, and they are quite glad their parents didn't opt for an abortion.<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm pretty pro-choice, but the idea that some people are better off never being allowed to live (save in the case where they have the most horrific of birth defects) is not an argument that I am comfortable seeing be made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T12:53:04-08:00","id":1010774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1010720-i-need-to-ask-something-highly-controversial-topic-please-be-patient-with-me?p=1010747#post1010747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Birth control should be freely accessible by everybody, and child-bearing people shouldn't be punished if the birth control doesn't work. Again: If a child-bearing person doesn't want a child, then they should not be forced to have a child for any reason, including mistakes.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also really important. My partner has a crippling fear of pregnancy and childbirth. Both them and their sibling were premature births, and they have a pretty small build, the last thing they want is to put another child through the same, not to mention the very real possibility of either them, the baby, or both dying (another one of their greatest fears). Knowing this, we are responsible. We take precautions, use birth control and contraceptives, which we are fortunate enough to be able to afford. But no form of birth control is 100% effective. It is entirely possible, despite our best efforts to the contrary, for them to become pregnant. If that were to happen, they would be in a position to decide whether to put themselves and our potential future child at serious risk to both of their lives, as well as putting both through something that would likely be life-alteringly traumatic for both of them. Or, to abort the pregnancy while it is still a cluster of cells that would be incapable of surviving independently from them. That is not a choice they would be able to make lightly, and it's not a choice that either of us would ever want them to have to make. But, I would respect their decision either way. And I would hope that if they decided to abort the pregnancy, it would be legal and safe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T12:53:35-08:00","id":1010775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1010720-i-need-to-ask-something-highly-controversial-topic-please-be-patient-with-me?p=1010765#post1010765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the kid cant regain the life they lost</div> </div> </div> </div>Though remember that some us don't think that they ever had a life to begin with. Thus it can't have its life taken away.<br /> <br /> But more importantly, nobody has the right to force child-bearers to bear children. You can disagree all you want, but making it illegal is even more immoral. This is also an issue that only affects child-bearing people: if you can't bear children, you're never going to be forced to make the decision. As somebody who can't bear children this is the sort of thing that will never affect me, so I don't believe I have a right to weigh in on it. Nor anybody else who can't bear children.<br /> <br /> And since what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3950_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3950\" data-vbnamecard=\"3950\">wonderandawe</a> said is also totally spot-on, nobody can know enough about a situation to pass judgment other than the child-bearer themselves and therefore policy shouldn't be made that makes the choice for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T12:59:10-08:00","id":1010778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1010720-i-need-to-ask-something-highly-controversial-topic-please-be-patient-with-me?p=1010771#post1010771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's kind of a dark argument. I know some people who were born to pretty brutal situations who have ended up having happy and successful lives, and they are quite glad their parents didn't opt for an abortion.<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm pretty pro-choice, but the idea that some people are better off never being allowed to live (save in the case where they have the most horrific of birth defects) is not an argument that I am comfortable seeing be made.</div> </div> </div> </div>Calling it &quot;never being allowed to live&quot; carries implications that living is something the potential child wants to do and is being denied. What ever side of the personhood question you fall on, you can't argue that a fetus at the stage of development where abortion is still a legal option has desires. Either way, the would-be mother is making a choice for their would-be child, that the would-be child has no say in. They can force the child to live in the situation they are born into, or they can stop it from being born. Either is a very serious decision to make for someone who can't make it for themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T13:03:24-08:00","id":1010781,"title":"","content":"My girlfriend has been pregnant for 18 weeks now so i have been reading and learning a few things.<br /> What i learned recently (tho its just a hearsay) is that there has been a law or rule enacted to clinics to no longer give their guest on the gender of the baby at the optional ultrasound taken between the 12th to 15th week (usually the gender is more certain at the ultrasound in the 20th week of pregnancy). Anyway apparently they discovered an increase in abortions following that first ultrasound.<br /> The relevance between the two isnt anything definitive and i certainly hope there is no correlation but i am a cynics and i guess there are people shitty enough to use gender as a reason for abortion.<br /> This is in Quebec (Canada) btw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T13:10:04-08:00","id":1010785,"title":"","content":"It's an ugly situation and I don't think there's any answer that will make people happy. To the extent I have an opinion that matters, I'm pro-choice because I view it as the option that causes the least harm.<br /> <br /> Something that bothers me a lot... Is the question of where we start counting the pregnancy as &quot;mattering&quot; in regards to whether there is a human life under consideration. Because if we say that there is a &quot;person&quot; involved at conception... This raises some very troublesome questions to answer. Supposedly, 30-40% of pregnancies miscarry in the first trimester, often before the pregnancy is even known about. <br /> <br /> How does that fit into viewing the fertilized egg or embryo as being a &quot;person&quot;?<br /> <br /> Some pro-life people argue that an abortion is murder. Would that mean a miscarriage is manslaughter?<br /> <br /> I don't think our legal system is really equipped to handle that. It goes weird places...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T13:16:38-08:00","id":1010786,"title":"","content":"I guess I can understand you guys now. You want the same thing I do, helping people. We just have different id\u00e9ias of how to get there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T13:42:03-08:00","id":1010793,"title":"","content":"The other thing is, by all accounts, banning abortion does <i>nothing</i> to prevent abortion. It just prevents <i>safe</i> ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T13:49:02-08:00","id":1010798,"title":"","content":"1. Pregnancy is a life-threatening condition. Pregnancy can cause diabetes, lactose intolerance, septic infections, infertility, heart disease, acute organ failue, suicidal depression, internal bleeding, osteoporosis, and death. In 2015, the mortality rate of pregnancy in Brazil was 44 per 100,000. That's not a huge number, but I prefer to live in a world where all of those people knew the risks and chose to proceed anyway. One of the things that keeps that number low is access to abortion.<br /> <br /> 2. Legalizing abortion reduces the number of abortions performed. Bringing things out of the shadows allows people to evaluate their decisions calmly and rationally, and seek outside resources they might not have discovered before. It also dramatically reduced the number of deaths from botched abortions to practically zero.<br /> <br /> 3. 33% of all fertiziled human ova fail to make it to term anyway. Anthropogenic abortion is a drop in the bucket compared to the natural version.<br /> <br /> 4. The actual ethical basis of the pro-choice argument is called &quot;bodily autonomy&quot;. Suppose for a moment that there is a genius kid out there who is on track to cure cancer and is suffering from acute kidney failure and you are the only match <i>in the entire world</i>. Even if they could do it with 100% success, no one has the right to hook you up to the kid and use your kidneys to keep them alive. And even if such an arrangement were made, you would be well within your rights to walk away and let him die. And once he was dead, no one could force his family to use his body to for science or any other purpose. His corpse is his own to dispense with as with all his other earthly affects.<br /> <br /> So <i>even if you accept the premise that a fertilized egg is a person</i>, the anti-abortion stance is that a fetus has more rights than a man, and that a woman has fewer rights than a corpse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T13:50:55-08:00","id":1010799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1010720-i-need-to-ask-something-highly-controversial-topic-please-be-patient-with-me?p=1010793#post1010793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other thing is, by all accounts, banning abortion does <i>nothing</i> to prevent abortion. It just prevents <i>safe</i> ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah.<br /> <br /> I learned fairly recently my state had a eugenics program that sterilized people the state decided they didn't want reproducing because their children might become a burden on the state. It was often done without actually telling the women what they were in for. The same state, North Carolina, is also falling back into increasingly anti-abortion prohibitions, limiting abortions to places only with helicopter pads, for instance, or requiring anyone who is getting one to get a sonogram first, that must be filed with the government, putting the whole thing behind a curtain of bureaucracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-01-2016, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T14:41:33-08:00","id":1010827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1010720-i-need-to-ask-something-highly-controversial-topic-please-be-patient-with-me?p=1010765#post1010765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The choice she had to make was either wrecking her Life or taking away the Life of another. I still think she didnt made a Good choice. All the things that would have happened to herbif she cart\u00f5es the birth could be fixed she could have dodged the guy, she could have solved it somehow it's a huge maybe but it's still possible. Theres no mayb,for the kid no other possibility. The kid has no Life and thats it.<br /> S\u00f3 if the choice is wrecking your Life or aborting. Wreck it. your Life can be fixed,the kid cant regain the life they lost</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm sure if she chose to, she could have found a way to make it work. Yet it wasn't my choice to make nor was it my life to wreck. It was hers. Thus it was her choice. As her friend, I choose to support her no matter what she choose.<br /> <br /> If I go to hell for that, so be it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T14:49:37-08:00","id":1010834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1010720-i-need-to-ask-something-highly-controversial-topic-please-be-patient-with-me?p=1010827#post1010827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm sure if she chose to, she could have found a way to make it work. Yet it wasn't my choice to make nor was it my life to wreck. It was hers. Thus it was her choice. As her friend, I choose to support her no matter what she choose.<br /> <br /> If I go to hell for that, so be it.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't presume knowing Gods's will. But i really dont think you or her are going to hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T14:54:48-08:00","id":1010837,"title":"","content":"A lot of what I would start with as already been said, so I'm going to start up a very different side of this:<br /> <br /> The anti-abortion movement as it exists in my country (the US) and many similar movements in other countries are - while not purposefully so - an attempt to force majority religious values on my religion.<br /> <br /> See, my faith has a very long standing view on abortion that does not match the &quot;personhood starts are conception, and abortion is murder,&quot; rhetoric. Supporting reproductive choice is also supporting members of my religion to practice our faith's teachings rather than another faith's teachings (since this is where the majority of anti-abortion stances are founded).<br /> <br /> One of the important aspects of this, is that even with my faith's views of personhood, we view abortion after fetal personhood as more nuanced than it is often treated. Once you accept the fetus is a person, you accept it has autonomy. Killing a fetus might be murder, but it might also be self-defense. That's actually the theological argument my faith falls on. An abortion after fetal personhood is acceptable if it follows our concept of self-defense. As well, my faith does not exactly view self defense as a choice. Your life is sacred, and you therefore have a religious obligation to protect it from others that through malice or ignorance would threaten it.<br /> <br /> So for women of my faith, if they've carried a child to the point we consider when a fetus develops personhood (which is later than conception), and she is of the valid belief that her child is posing a threat to her, she doesn't just have the right to defend herself, she has a moral obligation to do so. Obviously, it's never that simple, but that's something my faith teaches on this matter.<br /> <br /> So I come at the pro-choice side from a considerably different direction than most people. Pro-choice for me is not just a mater of bodily autonomy (though I do consider that important) but defending the right to have different moral considerations on abortion and choose according to those different beliefs.<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> <br /> On a separate note I want to push back against the, &quot;the mother should ruin her life for the sake of one child,&quot; argument.<br /> <br /> Consider for a moment that a mother that chooses to not ruin her life for one child who would then have to grow up living a very rough life, might then go on to have multiple children when she's ready to provide a proper stable home for them. If we're thinking in terms of the theoretical potential of an unborn child, how do you weigh protecting the theoretical life of one child, to the theoretical lives of three other children the mother could have if she didn't have the first?<br /> <br /> It's a horrible choice to have to make of course. In a perfect world she could have all four children. But this world is not perfect. Once you start arguing for the potential life of a child, you open the room to discuss the potential life of every other child that mother might have. If you force a mother into a situation where having more kids later isn't feasible (or even possible) for her, you're saying having a pregnancy to term is actually more important than all those kids.<br /> <br /> And while I am phrasing this as a hypothetical, it's really not for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T15:27:07-08:00","id":1010843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1010720-i-need-to-ask-something-highly-controversial-topic-please-be-patient-with-me?p=1010837#post1010837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, my faith has a very long standing view on abortion that does not match the &quot;personhood starts are conception, and abortion is murder,&quot; rhetoric. Supporting reproductive choice is also supporting members of my religion to practice our faith's teachings rather than another faith's teachings (since this is where the majority of anti-abortion stances are founded).<br /> <br /> One of the important aspects of this, is that even with my faith's views of personhood, we view abortion after fetal personhood as more nuanced than it is often treated. Once you accept the fetus is a person, you accept it has autonomy. Killing a fetus might be murder, but it might also be self-defense. That's actually the theological argument my faith falls on. An abortion after fetal personhood is acceptable if it follows our concept of self-defense. As well, my faith does not exactly view self defense as a choice. Your life is sacred, and you therefore have a religious obligation to protect it from others that through malice or ignorance would threaten it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very interesting perspective on it, I never knew. My Sunday school never got to that point and I stopped practicing.<br /> <br /> My own view has been appreciating that at a certain point it is life, but sometimes it's a choice that has to be made anyways. Though I think most abortions are done fairly early, like first first trimester, where I wouldn't consider it a person to begin with. I think there's an idea out there that at that point it's just a regular baby, but smaller, inside people. This is based on my observation of sexual education in our country and a pamphlet I was given at my middle school by anti-abortion activists who were shoo'd off by security shortly afterward, which depicted a smiling baby being mutilated in a variety of ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T16:21:38-08:00","id":1010861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1010720-i-need-to-ask-something-highly-controversial-topic-please-be-patient-with-me?p=1010837#post1010837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I come at the pro-choice side from a considerably different direction than most people. Pro-choice for me is not just a mater of bodily autonomy (though I do consider that important) but defending the right to have different moral considerations on abortion and choose according to those different beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a fascinating argument I've never seen before on this topic. Thank you for sharing that. It's helped me think about this topic in a different way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T16:39:18-08:00","id":1010866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1010720-i-need-to-ask-something-highly-controversial-topic-please-be-patient-with-me?p=1010827#post1010827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm sure if she chose to, she could have found a way to make it work. Yet it wasn't my choice to make nor was it my life to wreck. It was hers. Thus it was her choice. As her friend, I choose to support her no matter what she choose.<br /> <br /> If I go to hell for that, so be it.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;All right, then, I'll go to hell.&quot; - Huckleberry Finn<br /> <br /> One of the most powerful quotes I know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T21:50:11-08:00","id":1010930,"title":"","content":"Much of my own views have been echoed by others. I want to live in a world where abortions don't happen. But I sure don't want to live in a world where they're made illegal/inaccessible to achieve that goal. <br /> <br /> I am a very firm supporter of mandatory sex education, and free birth control for any that want it, not just because of the abortion angle but because repeated studies have shown that planning parenthood rather than it being a whoops situation has a positive impact not only on the children that are born but on the parents. It's a cheap price for greater stability and economic gains for a country.<br /> <br /> More importantly, I've read and researched enough of what USED to happen in the western cultures. Women taking crazy risks, abusing themselves, poisoning themselves, all in an effort to get the fetus to abort because it would ruin their lives. Or back when it was a family scale disaster, women who would get disappeared for a year or so and quickly married off when they come back. Or arranging for &quot;treatment&quot; of &quot;a female disorder&quot; by a hysterectomy. There have been more than a few suicides over becoming pregnant.<br /> <br /> Making it illegal... is actively counterproductive. Not only is it punishing someone that actively feels they have no alternative... think about it, would you trust a random guy who washed out of medical school to perform a back-street procedure on you if you thought there was a reasonable choice? Not only that, but it drives home the concept that sex by virtue of pregnancy is bad/evil/wrong unless you're prepared to have a baby. So yay shaming people for stuff they're biologically driven to do anyway.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T01:31:51-08:00","id":1010977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1010720-i-need-to-ask-something-highly-controversial-topic-please-be-patient-with-me#post1010720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay,i need to vent a bit and if any of you guys could answer that'd be fine. So, all cards on the table. I'm anti-abortion. i tried not to be but the truth is. When i see an abortion,i see a little kind being thrown in thrash-bin. I see . My country,Brazil, had some reviews our laws this week. it was bad,but one law i do agree with is the Criminizalition of abortion unless the pregnancy directs threatens the woman's life. It is hard for me seeing so many people railing against politicians who voted for that. Especially because those people didnt attack politicians who did worse. And it's hard for me to understand something about pro-choice people. Why do you think people who are against abortion are just trying to hurt women? every single pro-choice argument i've sen always says &amp;quot;you don't care about women,You just want to hurt women&amp;quot;. And that's just isn't the reality. Based on my experiences almost all pro-life people are coming from the same idea. That a fetus is a human being, or at the very least will become a human being and that we shouldn't let people just thrown them away like that. I'm still trying to understand pro-choice to empathize with them. that's why i'm asking this here,please be patient with.<br /> <br /> Why is there a belief that pro-life people about trying to hurt woman and not about saving lifes, or at the very least things that will be alive after some months?</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm very prochoice, I support state funded abortions. That being said I don't believe antiabortion people are mysgonists, but ignorant social conservatives.<br /> <br /> Look for the first two trimesters its a glorified clump of cells. You're letting your imagination get the best of you. They are not people, the change to fetus to child begins in the third trimester and ends with birth.<br /> <br /> And third trimester abortions are relatively rare and usually do to extreme circumstances.<br /> <br /> Do you get bent over the lose of potential life every time you masturbate, of course not.<br /> <br /> You just have an over active imagination is all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T04:27:34-08:00","id":1011009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1010720-i-need-to-ask-something-highly-controversial-topic-please-be-patient-with-me#post1010720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why is there a belief that pro-life people about trying to hurt woman and not about saving lifes, or at the very least things that will be alive after some months?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bProbably because in the US the same people that are pro-life tend not to support the idea of helping the parent(s) after the child is born (via tax supported government assistance) and in fact vilify those parents for relying on any taxpayer funded assistance they can get. You know, the people that complain about all the tax dollars that go to welfare, even though that amount is a miniscule amount of the annual federal budget. Oddly enough they also tend to support the death penalty while talking about the sanctity of life. Let's see those same people start adopting kids with expensive medical conditions, kids who aren't babies/toddlers, or kids who aren't the same race and I'll start to change my opinion of them. It's been my experience that these same people are the ones that don't want the government intruding into their lives and decisions but have no problem forcing their opinions and religious beliefs on others by seeking to legislate those beliefs. Then you have the issue of those same people being against the idea of gay couples adopting, they'd rather see a child live as a ward of the state than have parents that don't fit their idea of what a real family should look like. It's just one set of hypocritical views after another IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 12-02-2016, 07:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T04:52:29-08:00","id":1011016,"title":"","content":"Just the fact of being Pro-death penalty while saying they are Pro-life is a sick joke that makes imposible to sympatize with their claims.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T06:27:00-08:00","id":1011039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1010720-i-need-to-ask-something-highly-controversial-topic-please-be-patient-with-me?p=1010837#post1010837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I come at the pro-choice side from a considerably different direction than most people. Pro-choice for me is not just a mater of bodily autonomy (though I do consider that important) but defending the right to have different moral considerations on abortion and choose according to those different beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's important to note, BTW, that <i>Roe v. Wade</i>, the U.S. court case that legalized abortion nationwide <i>was not controversial when it was made</i>. The SCOTUS of the time had 3 justices regarded as Conservative, 3 regarded as Liberal, and 3 regarded as Moderate. The Majority opinion was written by a Conservative and the Dissenting opinion was written by a Liberal. Both Dissenters agreed that abortion should be legal but disagreed that there was a Constitutional argument for it.<br /> <br /> Abortion only became a controversial issue (in the US) in the 80s when Conservatives needed a wedge issue to Get Out The Vote. <i>That</i> is when the notion that personhood began at conception was invented.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.huffingtonpost.com/jonathan-dudley/how-evangelicals-decided-that-life-begins-at-conception_b_2072716.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://img.huffingtonpost.com/asset/default-entry.jpg?ops=1200_630\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.huffingtonpost.com/jonathan-dudley/how-evangelicals-decided-that-life-begins-at-conception_b_2072716.html\" target=\"_blank\"> How Evangelicals Decided That Life Begins At Conception </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.huffingtonpost.com/jonathan-dudley/how-evangelicals-decided-that-life-begins-at-conception_b_2072716.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.huffingtonpost.com/jonathan-dudley/how-evangelicals-decided-that-life-begins-at-conception_b_2072716.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> In the late 1960s and early 1970s, evangelical Christians widely believed the Bible says life begins at birth and supported looser abortion policies. Given current evangelical anti-abortion activism, the reality and significance of this history deserves fuller discussion. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T09:14:50-08:00","id":1011110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1010720-i-need-to-ask-something-highly-controversial-topic-please-be-patient-with-me?p=1011009#post1011009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bProbably because in the US the same people that are pro-life tend not to support the idea of helping the parent(s) after the child is born (via tax supported government assistance) and in fact vilify those parents for relying on any taxpayer funded assistance they can get. You know, the people that complain about all the tax dollars that go to welfare, even though that amount is a miniscule amount of the annual federal budget. Oddly enough they also tend to support the death penalty while talking about the sanctity of life. Let's see those same people start adopting kids with expensive medical conditions, kids who aren't babies/toddlers, or kids who aren't the same race and I'll start to change my opinion of them. It's been my experience that these same people are the ones that don't want the government intruding into their lives and decisions but have no problem forcing their opinions and religious beliefs on others by seeking to legislate those beliefs. Then you have the issue of those same people being against the idea of gay couples adopting, they'd rather see a child live as a ward of the state than have parents that don't fit their idea of what a real family should look like. It's just one set of hypocritical views after another IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is rather a bit of tarring everyone with the same brush I think. Not all the pro-life people I know support the death penalty, but a very vocal minority do. Likewise not all the people that are pro-life that I've encountered are opposed to social support programmes. Again, the very vocal ones stand out and it's easy to assume the ones you hear about the most are the ones that make up the majority, but that is often not the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T09:22:33-08:00","id":1011111,"title":"","content":"I think pointing out what seems to be a philosophical inconsistency in the rhetoric, I wouldn't take it as an attack against those for whom it doesn't apply. It certainly is a point to be made to those that think it does apply, and that's not a small number of people.<br /> <br /> I think one thing that people need to consider about the whole &quot;anti-abortion=anti-woman&quot; thing is that they have to understand that not as a personal attack or some kind of ad-hominem, but as the result of a behavior, a consequence of it. The anti-woman-ness of opposition abortion rights is not necessarily about what you THINK or FEEL but about what the PRACTICE of your opinion may result in for the women whose access to abortion resources are restricted or stigmatized.<br /> <br /> I don't care to say anybody is a bad person for feeling this way or that way about it, because I definitely understand the fundamental philosophical issue, and why for many people who are anti-abortion they feel a moral obligation to try to enact policy to support their view. I just want people to consider that the notion of being &quot;anti-woman&quot; here is not about your mean thoughts or supposed mean thoughts, but about your actions and their practical consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 12-02-2016, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T11:47:12-08:00","id":1011156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1010720-i-need-to-ask-something-highly-controversial-topic-please-be-patient-with-me?p=1011039#post1011039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abortion only became a controversial issue (in the US) in the 80s when Conservatives needed a wedge issue to Get Out The Vote. <i>That</i> is when the notion that personhood began at conception was invented.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that's a somewhat shallow reading of history. The current anti-abortion movement in the US started directly in response to Roe v. Wade, it just didn't get mainstream political power until later as a voting bloc the conservative movements were willing to court in the 80s.<br /> <br /> It's also neglecting a very long history of abortion being illegal (before Roe, 30 states flatly outlawed abortion, and 16 made abortion illegal with specific exceptions), where it wasn't really controversial to be anti-abortion because the majority of the country was anti-abortion in the eyes of the law. The few states with legal abortion without government interference and the long standing underground abortion practices where highly controversial; but they were not seen as national level issues.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1010720-i-need-to-ask-something-highly-controversial-topic-please-be-patient-with-me?p=1011110#post1011110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is rather a bit of tarring everyone with the same brush I think. Not all the pro-life people I know support the death penalty, but a very vocal minority do. Likewise not all the people that are pro-life that I've encountered are opposed to social support programmes. Again, the very vocal ones stand out and it's easy to assume the ones you hear about the most are the ones that make up the majority, but that is often not the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's a certain amount of acceptable tarring here. In addition to the excellent points <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"159\" data-vbnamecard=\"159\">Leetsepeak</a> made:<br /> <br /> The biggest issue is that the forces <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11\" data-vbnamecard=\"11\">Darksider</a> talks about operate together as a political entity. Even if individual groups and people are for or against only part of those clusters of issues, the political power is concentrated by clustering those issues together into a single powerful voting bloc. There is a very big difference between what people individually personally believe, and what they feel needs to be in the law.. The people that choose to actively advocate against legal abortion (as opposed to people that simply would not personally get an abortion regardless of the risks and don't want to force that decision on others), are at a minimum in political bed with the death penalty advocates, the movement to eliminate/further restrict government assistance programs, the movements against &quot;non-traditional&quot; families being allowed to adopt, allowing &quot;small government&quot; funding cuts to reduce funding to public adoption agencies and the foster care systems, advocate insufficient or no sex-ed, etc.<br /> <br /> However much a minority these people might be in numerically, they're not a minor group in terms of politics and law.<br /> <br /> I know a lot of people that are personally anti-abortion for a number of reasons, but wholly believe in voting pro-choice because they recognize their position is a choice that shouldn't be forced on others, and they frequently express very similar feelings about the larger anti-abortion movement: that it isn't really about &quot;life&quot; because it doesn't push for the value of all life over the value of forcing pregnancies to be carried to term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T12:35:52-08:00","id":1011170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1010720-i-need-to-ask-something-highly-controversial-topic-please-be-patient-with-me?p=1011016#post1011016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just the fact of being Pro-death penalty while saying they are Pro-life is a sick joke that makes imposible to sympatize with their claims.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've heard similar statements from people on the right, about what a sick joke liberal's views are, how they oppose the death penalty while accepting abortion - that they value the lives of convicted murderers while turning a blind eye to the murder of unborn babies, so it's impossible to sympathize with anything liberals say.<br /> <br /> And, to be fair to those people, they believe that there''s a big difference between allowing private citizens to kill someone <i>before</i> they have a chance to be born, and supporting the ability of the state to execute someone <i>after</i> they have committed a horrific crime, been found guilty by a jury of their peers, and had the chance (sometimes multiple times) to try and appeal that verdict to a higher court.<br /> <br /> But then I'm someone who supports abortion and supports the death penalty, so I approach the table with the idea that abortion and the death penalty are two very different and very complex situations that are only superficially similar on the surface. So I don't think there's a schism in the thinking of those who oppose abortion and support the death penalty <b>or</b> in those who support abortion and oppose the death penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 12-03-2016, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T11:35:22-08:00","id":1011594,"title":"","content":"Me personally I'd have no problem being described as &quot;pro-death.&quot; (Or dare I say it? A &quot;Deathist.&quot;) It's a pretty accurate description of my politics. I'm pro-abortion, pro-death penalty, and fairly hawkish in my foreign policy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T12:02:17-08:00","id":1011603,"title":"","content":"My primary objection to the death penalty is that you can't un-execute someone if it turns out they were innocent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T14:29:26-08:00","id":1011667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1010720-i-need-to-ask-something-highly-controversial-topic-please-be-patient-with-me?p=1011603#post1011603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My primary objection to the death penalty is that you can't un-execute someone if it turns out they were innocent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally agreed. I'm okay with the idea of a death penalty in theory, but the way the US currently implements is a no-go for me and certainly I think there needs to be reform in the when and how the death penalty is implemented (and a major reform of the US' criminal justice system and criminal justice philosophy altogether).<br /> <br /> I think the most important thing is that when deciding on a death penalty, the evidence needs to be higher than it normally is during a trial. During a trial someone is innocent unless there is &quot;cause beyond a reasonable doubt&quot; to find them guilty. But to inflict the death penalty, I think there needs to be a demand for an even higher level burden of proof - an &quot;absolute certainty&quot; that someone is guilty. Something such as a recording of the crime taking place or DNA evidence that renders the defendant's guilty to be definitive. <br /> <br /> Too many death sentence convictions are found based off of witness testimony or questionable forensic data and, like you say, we can't un-execute someone. So in the absence of that sort of &quot;hard proof,&quot; I don't believe the death penalty should even be an option on the table. But when such evidence can be presented by the prosecution I generally don't have an issue with those specific death penalty cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T16:15:47-08:00","id":1011719,"title":"","content":"I have weird views on prisons and the like.<br /> <br /> I am not a big proponent of a vengeance based penal system. I believe we should focus on rehabilitation. Having a percentage of the population locked up isn't a good idea. We need to reeducate them, find them productive work, and integrate them into society. This include those who have murdered, raped, etc. Prison right now teaches you to be a good criminal and/or prisoner. We should put serious effort and resources into teaching people how to live in the legal economy. <br /> <br /> However, if the prisoner has proven not to re-integrated into society (repeat murderers and the like), then I see no point in keeping them locked up for the rest of their life. If you are so twisted, society deems fit to lock you away for the rest of your life, well, maybe the rest of your life should be short. These are the people that the death penalty is designed for. <br /> <br /> It's probably a naive point of view, but can't be any worse than what we have now. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}